        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - Crafting needs Engineering progression, a specialization and materials; a player purchase bypasses that work.\n\n1. Choose a route: buy Personal World Destroyer as an unused item or caged battle pet from another player, or craft it. Learn a purchased cage at its displayed pet-level requirement; no Engineering is needed for collection.\n\n2. For crafting, visit Lilliam Sparkspindle in Stormwind at 62.8,32.0 or Roxxik in Orgrimmar at 56.8,56.4. Learn Engineering and Cataclysm Engineering, then reach Cataclysm skill 25. If you lack the specialization, also raise the separate Classic Engineering skill to 200; Cataclysm skill does not replace that requirement.\n\n3. If not already a Goblin Engineer, take Goblin Engineering from the capital trainer on an eligible level 20+ character. Craft or buy 20 Big Iron Bombs, 20 Solid Dynamite and 5 Explosive Sheep and hand them in to unlock the specialization. Return to the trainer's recipe list and learn Personal World Destroyer. An existing specialist can craft it for you instead.\n\n4. Gather 10 Obsidium Bars, 8 Handfuls of Obsidium Bolts and 8 Electrified Ether. Bolts are crafted from Obsidium Bars and Electrified Ether from Volatile Air. Bring the High-Powered Bolt Gun and Blacksmith Hammer tools required by the recipe, or valid replacements for those tools.\n\n5. At an anvil, craft Personal World Destroyer and use the finished item. A specialist can also craft it for you from your materials, avoiding the need to level or change your own profession.",
