        itemId = 66080,
        name = "Tiny Flamefly",
        stepCount = 6,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - A long, branching quest chain with disguise and automatic follow-ups, but no random drop.\n\n1. Start at Flamestar Post near 17.3,51.5 in Burning Steppes. Work with Mouton Flamestar and John J. Keeshan (Alliance) or Ariok (Horde): Done Nothing Wrong, Burning Vengeance, Stocking Up, A Future Project and Mud Hunter.\n\n2. Continue The Sand, the Cider, and the Orb to Gorzeeki Wildeyes near 8.3,35.9. Finish Warlocks Have the Neatest Stuff and Shadow Boxing, return to your faction contact, then follow Chiselgrip, the Heart of the Steppes.\n\n3. At Chiselgrip around 46,44, complete Stebben's Prove Yer Allegiance, Scrapped Golems and Golem Training. Continue the main infiltration chain through A Needle in a Hellhole, A Perfect Costume and Into the Black Tooth Hovel.\n\n4. While disguised, finish Strategic Cuts, Grunt Work, The Kodocaller's Horn and Taking the Horn for Ourselves. Continue General Thorg'izog and Trial by Magma. Accept the automatic Abuse of Power follow-up and finish Enough Damage for One Day.\n\n5. Alliance: follow Morgan's Vigil to Oralius at 71.8,67.9 and accept SEVEN! YUP!. Horde: follow Flame Crest to Kibler at 54.9,22.5 and accept Not Fireflies, Flameflies. Dismiss critter-eating companions before collecting seven nearby sparkling Flameflies by clicking them.\n\n6. Turn in to your faction's quest giver, take Tiny Flamefly and learn it. This companion cannot be caged. A low Booty Bay reputation can prevent Horde interaction with Kibler; use a character without that hostility or repair its reputation.",
