        itemId = 66067,
        name = "Singing Sunflower",
        stepCount = 5,
        acquisition = "Difficulty: Medium - The final garden-defense waves require resource management and timely rebuilding.\n\n1. Visit Brazie the Botanist at 33.6,49.5 in Hillsbrad Foothills, south of the Dalaran Crater. Finish Basic Botany, Flower Power, Ghouls Hate My Grains and Someone Setup the Pumpkin Bomb, then accept Lawn of the Dead.\n\n2. Start each round by collecting sunpower and planting Sunflowers in the leftmost column. Add Spitters in lanes with approaching enemies, using Rocknuts ahead of them to buy time. Expand toward two Sunflower columns without leaving an attacked lane undefended.\n\n3. Build damage and slowing plants in front of the Sunflowers: Spitters, Freezyas and, once available, Strangler Vines. Replace damaged front plants as cooldowns allow. Vines can reach nearby lanes; they do not need to occupy the enemy-entry squares.\n\n4. During the final fight, save enough sunpower for Pumpkin Bombs and replacement Sunflowers. Bomb Warden Stillwater and clustered tough enemies when the bomb is ready. Rebuild plants destroyed by his attacks so both income and lane defenses continue.\n\n5. Survive until the objective completes, turn in Lawn of the Dead to Brazie, and use Brazie's Sunflower Seeds. Search the journal for Singing Sunflower. You do not need an unavailable endless-mode achievement for the pet.",
        wowheadUrl = "https://www.wowhead.com/item=66067",
    },
